  "response_complete": true,
  "response_text": "Recurrent headaches with light sensitivity can be a sign of a more serious condition, such as migraines or other neurological disorders. It is important to seek medical attention if you experience these symptoms, as they can be a sign of a more serious condition. Some warning signs to watch for include:\n\n  1. Severe or persistent headaches that do not improve with over-the-counter pain medication.\n  2. Headaches that are accompanied by other symptoms, such as nausea, vomiting, or sensitivity to light and sound.\n  3. Headaches that are accompanied by other neurological symptoms, such as weakness, numbness, or tingling in the limbs.\n  4. Headaches that are accompanied by other symptoms, such as difficulty speaking, vision problems, or difficulty walking.\n  5. Headaches that are accompanied by other symptoms, such as a stiff neck or fever.\n\nIf you experience any of these warning signs, it is important to seek medical attention as soon as possible. Your doctor may recommend a variety of treatments, including medication, lifestyle changes, and other therapies, to help manage your symptoms and prevent future headaches.",
